# COMMERCE ENGINE v2 — Refined Product Vision

> **North Star**: "Can a clothing seller from Narayanganj set this up on her ৳8,000 Android phone in 5 minutes, and manage her entire business from it daily?"

---

## Critical Flaws in the Previous Plan (Fixed Below)

> [!WARNING]
> ### Technical Flaws
> 1. **No Auth Strategy** — Previous plan had no concrete auth system. Now using Firebase Phone OTP (already set up) + Supabase for data. This is the correct BD-first approach.
> 2. **Subdomain Routing on Vercel is Fragile** — Wildcard SSL, cold starts, and custom domain verification are all pain points. Need a robust middleware + DNS verification flow.
> 3. **No Caching Layer** — Multi-tenant SaaS without caching = every store hits the DB on every request. Need ISR + edge caching per tenant.
> 4. **No Version History / Undo** — Visual builder without undo = merchants destroying their own sites. Must have revision history.
> 5. **JSON Page Blocks Without Schema Validation** — Raw JSON is fragile. Need Zod schemas per block type to prevent corruption.
> 6. **No API Layer** — No mention of REST/webhook APIs for third-party integrations (courier, accounting, POS).
> 7. **No Data Export / Portability** — Merchants fear vendor lock-in. Must offer CSV/JSON export of all their data.
> 8. **No Rate Limiting or Abuse Prevention** — Free tier without limits = abuse. Need per-store request throttling.

> [!WARNING]
> ### Business & Feature Flaws
> 1. **No Staff/Team Accounts** — Real businesses have employees. Need role-based access (Owner, Manager, Staff).
> 2. **No Blog/Content System** — SEO-driven organic traffic requires a blog. Every competitor has this.
> 3. **No Multi-Language Storefront** — Plan only mentions Bengali admin UI, not customer-facing multi-language.
> 4. **No Migration Tools** — The #1 barrier to switching CMS is fear of data loss. Need import from eBitans/WooCommerce/Shopify CSV.
> 5. **No Tax/VAT Handling** — BD has VAT requirements. Ignoring this loses enterprise customers.
> 6. **No Subscription/Recurring Products** — Missing an entire product type (meal plans, monthly boxes).
> 7. **Pricing Too Cheap** — ৳299 Basic plan with 200 products and custom domain is unsustainable. Revised below.
> 8. **No Community or Education** — Merchants need hand-holding. No learning center, no community forum.

---

## Refined Architecture

### Auth System (Firebase + Supabase Hybrid)
```
Firebase Auth (Phone OTP + Google + Facebook)
        ↓ (on sign-in)
Supabase JWT Custom Token (via Edge Function)
        ↓
Supabase RLS (all data queries use store_id from JWT)
```
- **Why Firebase for Auth**: Phone OTP is native, reliable, and free for BD phone numbers. Supabase phone auth has regional SMS delivery issues.
- **Why Supabase for Data**: Postgres + RLS is the best multi-tenant data layer. Keep all business data here.
- **The Bridge**: A Supabase Edge Function verifies the Firebase ID token and issues a Supabase JWT with `store_id` embedded in the claims.

### Multi-Tenant Routing (Hardened)
```
Request → Vercel Edge Middleware
  ├─ Extract hostname
  ├─ Query edge-cached store config (KV store or ISR)
  ├─ Inject store_id into request headers
  └─ Rewrite to /_tenant/[store_slug]/[...path]

App Router reads store_id from headers
  ├─ Server Components fetch tenant-scoped data
  ├─ CSS variables injected from store_themes table
  └─ ISR caches pages per-tenant (revalidate on edit)
```

### Database Schema (Expanded)

```sql
-- === MULTI-TENANCY CORE ===
stores (
  id UUID PK, owner_id, name, slug UNIQUE, custom_domain,
  plan TEXT, store_type TEXT, logo_url, favicon_url,
  is_published BOOL, created_at, updated_at
)

-- === TEAM & PERMISSIONS ===
store_members (
  id, store_id FK, user_id FK, role ENUM('owner','manager','staff'),
  permissions JSONB, invited_at, accepted_at
)

-- === THEMING ===
store_themes (
  store_id FK UNIQUE, template_id,
  colors JSONB,        -- {primary, secondary, accent, background, text, success, error}
  typography JSONB,    -- {headingFont, bodyFont, sizeScale}
  components JSONB,    -- {buttonRadius, buttonStyle, cardStyle, imageRatio}
  custom_css TEXT,
  animations_enabled BOOL DEFAULT true
)

-- === PAGE BUILDER ===
store_pages (id, store_id FK, slug, title, is_homepage BOOL, seo_title, seo_description)

store_page_blocks (
  id, page_id FK, store_id FK,
  block_type TEXT NOT NULL,   -- validated against enum
  props JSONB NOT NULL,       -- validated by Zod schema per block_type
  sort_order INT, is_visible BOOL,
  created_at, updated_at
)

-- VERSION HISTORY (undo/redo)
store_page_revisions (
  id, page_id FK, store_id FK,
  blocks_snapshot JSONB,      -- full snapshot of all blocks
  changed_by UUID, created_at,
  revision_label TEXT         -- "Auto-save", "Published", etc.
)

-- === PRODUCTS (multi-tenant) ===
products (id, store_id FK, name, slug, description, base_price, compare_price,
  category_id FK, images JSONB, status ENUM, product_type ENUM,
  seo_title, seo_description, weight, dimensions JSONB,
  is_digital BOOL, digital_file_url, created_at, updated_at)

product_variants (id, product_id FK, store_id FK, sku, price, stock,
  attributes JSONB, image_url, is_active BOOL)

-- === ORDERS ===
orders (id, store_id FK, order_number, customer_id FK,
  items JSONB, subtotal, discount, delivery_fee, tax, total,
  payment_method, payment_status ENUM, payment_proof_url,
  shipping_address JSONB, shipping_status ENUM,
  courier_provider, tracking_number, notes TEXT,
  created_at, updated_at)

-- === CUSTOMERS ===
customers (id, store_id FK, name, phone, email, address JSONB,
  tags TEXT[], total_orders INT, total_spent NUMERIC,
  loyalty_points INT, notes TEXT, created_at)

-- === BLOG / CONTENT ===
blog_posts (id, store_id FK, title, slug, content TEXT,
  featured_image, status ENUM, seo_title, seo_description,
  published_at, created_at)

-- === ANALYTICS (lightweight) ===
store_events (id, store_id FK, event_type TEXT,
  metadata JSONB, session_id, referrer, created_at)
```

