## Key Technical Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| **Auth** | Firebase (Phone OTP) + Supabase (data) | BD users expect phone login. Firebase has best OTP delivery. |
| **Database** | Supabase Postgres + RLS | Multi-tenant isolation without separate DBs. Cost-effective. |
| **Framework** | Next.js 16 App Router | Server Components reduce JS bundle for low-end phones. |
| **Styling** | Tailwind + CSS Variables | CSS vars for per-store theming. Tailwind for dev speed. |
| **State (Builder)** | Zustand | Lightweight, perfect for real-time preview state. |
| **Image CDN** | Cloudinary | Auto WebP, responsive sizes, watermarking API. |
| **Hosting** | Vercel | Edge network, ISR support, easy custom domains. |
| **Page Builder Schema** | Zod-validated JSON | Type-safe block props. Prevents data corruption. |
| **Push Notifications** | Firebase Cloud Messaging | Already in the stack. Works with PWA. |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **The Single Most Important Metric**: Time-to-First-Sale. Every feature, every UX decision, every onboarding step should be optimized to get a merchant from "I heard about this platform" to "I just received my first order" in the shortest time possible. That is the moment they become a paying, loyal customer.

> [!TIP]
> **Launch Strategy**: Don't build all 12 templates. Launch with 3 (Clothing, Food, General). Get 20 real BD merchants using it. Watch them on their phones. Fix what confuses them. Then expand. Your first 20 users will teach you more than 6 months of planning.
